        "username": "The_Justifier",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/the_justifier/{size}/4954_2.png",
        "created_at": "2021-09-16T20:01:51.122Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Which makes the ebay price jacking even more contemptible.</p>\n<p>What I wonder most about isn’t the old promos like RC Wraith, it’s the ones that postdate the release of the two variant collections, such as hero Infinitor and Omnitron-U.  I know that Adam made an art for the “normal” versions of these, but I have no idea if they were ever even printed, let alone distributed.  The first time I saw them announce OU, it was with the art that his* promo version uses, where he’s standing in the kind of hunched position and looking right; the only time I’ve ever seen the art with him staying straight and turning his head was in the video game.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>I know that O-X prefers the pronoun “it”, but using this is a recipe for unintelligible sentences at the best of times, and we’re discussing a piece of card art here, so referring to the picture as “it” and the character as “him” makes for better clarity.</li>\n</ul>",
        "post_number": 5,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-09-16T20:01:51.122Z",
        "reply_count": 1,
        "reply_to_post_number": 4,
